    "result_text": "The full build succeeds (the project's Surefire config runs the acceptance suite). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` field following the existing pattern for computed owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`MembershipTierFormatter`** (new util) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class, mirroring `MembershipNumberFormatter`, that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount` is `0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`. Null-safe on both inputs.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added one expression `@Mapping` delegating to the new formatter, consistent with how the other derived fields are wired.\n\nNo existing logic was duplicated or bloated. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
